00:00:00,010 --> 00:01:33,930
[ Watch on kissFlix.co ]

1
00:00:47,777 --> 00:00:51,072
THE APARTMENT JOB

2
00:00:52,824 --> 00:00:54,492
I haven't introduced myself properly.

3
00:00:59,289 --> 00:01:00,999
I'm the president of Taesan Construction,

4
00:01:01,875 --> 00:01:03,001
Lee Chung-won.

5
00:01:17,432 --> 00:01:19,726
You seem to be great at finding things,

6
00:01:19,809 --> 00:01:21,978
so what are you looking for here
at Taesan Group?

7
00:01:23,021 --> 00:01:26,024
Whatever it is, I'm afraid
you won't be able to find it here.

8
00:01:26,983 --> 00:01:27,984
I feel sorry about that.

9
00:01:29,777 --> 00:01:31,988
No, I've already found it.

10
00:01:32,655 --> 00:01:35,700
You have control
over True Value's reserve fund.

11
00:01:35,783 --> 00:01:36,826
Come on.

12
00:01:37,702 --> 00:01:38,953
What do you mean?

13
00:01:40,496 --> 00:01:44,250
You got rid of President Seo,

14
00:01:44,334 --> 00:01:47,712
so you're making it difficult
for me to use my own money.

15
00:01:48,338 --> 00:01:50,048
I know I shouldn't,

16
00:01:50,632 --> 00:01:53,343
but I'm starting to resent you.

17
00:01:55,053 --> 00:01:57,263
<i>The moment I treat him like an enemy,</i>

18
00:01:57,347 --> 00:01:58,890
<i>the reserve fund goes out the window.</i>

19
00:01:59,557 --> 00:02:02,435
Then can't I just do

20
00:02:03,186 --> 00:02:05,939
what President Seo used to do?

21
00:02:08,900 --> 00:02:09,734
Why don't you

22
00:02:10,693 --> 00:02:13,905
let me become your right-hand man?

23
00:02:19,994 --> 00:02:21,537
My right-hand man?

24
00:02:22,121 --> 00:02:23,122
I'm quite competent.

25
00:02:23,206 --> 00:02:24,749
Of course.

26
00:02:24,832 --> 00:02:27,502
You became the president
by planting relics.

27
00:02:27,585 --> 00:02:29,796
Your planning, execution, and acting…

28
00:02:29,879 --> 00:02:31,798
I know how impressive you are.

29
00:02:31,881 --> 00:02:33,925
I'll be better than President Seo.

30
00:02:34,008 --> 00:02:37,053
President Seo was the keeper of my vault.

31
00:02:37,845 --> 00:02:40,473
Deposits, withdrawals,

32
00:02:40,556 --> 00:02:42,767
and moving money around.

33
00:02:42,850 --> 00:02:44,769
My keeper only has one job.

34
00:02:45,645 --> 00:02:47,105
To keep my money safe.

35
00:02:49,148 --> 00:02:50,191
That's

36
00:02:51,150 --> 00:02:52,068
it?

37
00:02:54,445 --> 00:02:56,531
But it's not an easy job.

38
00:02:56,614 --> 00:02:57,532
This place

39
00:02:57,615 --> 00:03:00,868
is filled with parasites
eating away at my fund.

40
00:03:00,952 --> 00:03:03,538
They're always asking for things.

41
00:03:04,706 --> 00:03:07,709
Why don't you give me a chance first,
then decide?

42
00:03:08,292 --> 00:03:09,335
How would I trust you?

43
00:03:10,545 --> 00:03:12,672
You came to empty out my vault.

44
00:03:13,881 --> 00:03:18,219
I only realized today
that the vault had an owner.

45
00:03:18,803 --> 00:03:19,887
And if there's an owner,

46
00:03:20,596 --> 00:03:22,015
I should suck up to them

47
00:03:23,266 --> 00:03:25,685
if I want to get any scraps.

48
00:03:27,186 --> 00:03:29,772
Okay. Then do as you like.

49
00:03:29,856 --> 00:03:33,818
I need to like you
to be able to trust you with my key.

50
00:03:34,527 --> 00:03:36,279
I don't work with just anyone.

51
00:03:48,708 --> 00:03:52,295
I can't believe the president here
was the penthouse jerk.

52
00:03:52,378 --> 00:03:54,297
You used to say you admired him.

53
00:03:54,797 --> 00:03:57,508
Taesan Construction really is huge.

54
00:03:59,510 --> 00:04:03,056
<i>Just wait and see how I take that key.</i>

55
00:04:08,686 --> 00:04:12,857
THE APARTMENT JOB

56
00:04:14,692 --> 00:04:16,486
It's past dinnertime,

57
00:04:16,569 --> 00:04:18,946
but no one's home yet.

58
00:04:19,030 --> 00:04:21,949
Preparing meals wasn't in my contract.

59
00:04:22,033 --> 00:04:23,576
Darn it.

60
00:04:23,659 --> 00:04:25,495
I can't believe I'm doing this at my age.

61
00:04:26,329 --> 00:04:28,164
Hey, come and eat!

62
00:04:29,165 --> 00:04:30,458
Okay!

63
00:04:31,626 --> 00:04:35,463
You're full of energy after your nap.

64
00:04:36,172 --> 00:04:38,341
-Thank you.
-Enjoy.

65
00:04:47,433 --> 00:04:48,267
<i>His wife?</i>

66
00:04:48,851 --> 00:04:50,728
Why are you the president's wife?

67
00:04:50,812 --> 00:04:53,064
What the hell have you been up to?

68
00:04:53,648 --> 00:04:55,400
Ha-jeong, just calm down.

69
00:04:56,025 --> 00:04:58,069
Mr. Park is actually my client--

70
00:04:58,152 --> 00:04:59,028
Client?

71
00:05:00,655 --> 00:05:01,656
This won't do.

72
00:05:01,739 --> 00:05:04,158
I'm going to take this up
with your law firm.

73
00:05:04,242 --> 00:05:07,120
You didn't take the bar exam
to pretend to be someone's mom.

74
00:05:07,203 --> 00:05:09,163
Why would they waste
your talent like this?

75
00:05:09,247 --> 00:05:11,541
Come on. I'll go talk to them.

76
00:05:11,624 --> 00:05:13,167
No, Ha-jeong.

77
00:05:13,251 --> 00:05:14,794
Come on. Hurry up.

78
00:05:15,503 --> 00:05:16,337
Ha-jeong.

79
00:05:17,922 --> 00:05:18,840
Ha-jeong…

80
00:05:19,674 --> 00:05:21,300
I'm not a lawyer.

81
00:05:24,679 --> 00:05:26,681
What are you talking about?

82
00:05:27,390 --> 00:05:28,933
You're not a lawyer?

83
00:05:29,851 --> 00:05:30,977
Let's go.

84
00:05:32,979 --> 00:05:34,063
I'm not.

85
00:05:36,190 --> 00:05:37,316
Kang Ha-ri.

86
00:05:38,025 --> 00:05:39,902
What are you, if you're not a lawyer?

87
00:05:39,986 --> 00:05:41,779
What are you, then?

88
00:05:42,280 --> 00:05:44,574
Tell me! What are you?

89
00:05:46,909 --> 00:05:49,787
Mom… I mean, Ha-ri. Come and eat.

90
00:05:53,916 --> 00:05:55,334
Geez.

91
00:05:55,418 --> 00:05:58,045
Your father-in-law
prepared dinner for you.

92
00:05:58,129 --> 00:06:00,381
At least pretend to have a bite.

93
00:06:00,464 --> 00:06:02,967
I don't have an appetite. Eat without me.

94
00:06:03,634 --> 00:06:06,470
Then just come
and have some eggs at least…

95
00:06:07,847 --> 00:06:10,266
Hey, you shouldn't have eaten
all that by yourself.

96
00:06:11,225 --> 00:06:14,729
Protein is important for growing children.

97
00:06:16,189 --> 00:06:17,690
Fine. Eat.

98
00:06:19,275 --> 00:06:21,110
You're not eating any soup, are you?

99
00:06:22,153 --> 00:06:23,779
The smell.

100
00:06:26,115 --> 00:06:27,533
I'm going home.

101
00:06:30,369 --> 00:06:31,954
Get home safely.

102
00:06:32,747 --> 00:06:35,124
Lizard, did something happen to her?

103
00:06:35,833 --> 00:06:39,086
I don't know. She's been like that
ever since picking up the kid.

104
00:06:39,587 --> 00:06:41,714
See that sunken spot on the sofa?

105
00:06:41,797 --> 00:06:43,966
She sat there all day,

106
00:06:44,050 --> 00:06:46,177
blankly staring out the window.

107
00:06:46,260 --> 00:06:48,387
Gyeong-buk,
is something going on with her?

108
00:06:50,598 --> 00:06:53,601
She just needs time to herself sometimes.

109
00:06:54,101 --> 00:06:56,187
Don't you even know that?

110
00:06:58,731 --> 00:07:01,484
If he knew,
he wouldn't be all alone, would he?

111
00:07:01,567 --> 00:07:02,693
Gyeong-buk's all grown up.

112
00:07:04,445 --> 00:07:06,447
Where are you, Yeong-ju?

113
00:07:06,530 --> 00:07:08,532
I opened a can since I was so frustrated.

114
00:07:09,033 --> 00:07:10,952
You'd better come before I'm done.

115
00:07:20,711 --> 00:07:22,296
<i>A stand-in service?</i>

116
00:07:23,839 --> 00:07:25,967
You're joking, right?

117
00:07:26,050 --> 00:07:27,260
That can't be true.

118
00:07:28,970 --> 00:07:31,889
I was given a job to play the role
of Park Hae-kang's wife.

119
00:07:35,393 --> 00:07:36,310
How…

120
00:07:39,021 --> 00:07:40,773
-How…
-Ha-jeong.

121
00:07:42,733 --> 00:07:45,653
How could you deceive me like this?

122
00:07:46,821 --> 00:07:49,490
I worked so hard
to help you become a lawyer.

123
00:07:49,574 --> 00:07:51,951
How could you do this to me?

124
00:07:52,910 --> 00:07:54,203
I never asked you to!

125
00:07:55,746 --> 00:07:58,958
Just stop.
I'm sick of hearing you say that!

126
00:08:00,668 --> 00:08:02,086
Don't do anything anymore.

127
00:08:02,169 --> 00:08:03,921
I know it's hard for you,

128
00:08:04,005 --> 00:08:06,424
so just don't do anything for me anymore!

129
00:08:13,848 --> 00:08:14,765
You're the worst.

130
00:08:19,437 --> 00:08:20,896
You're so shameless.

131
00:08:21,564 --> 00:08:22,481
You're…

132
00:08:24,150 --> 00:08:25,860
seriously messed up.

133
00:08:29,822 --> 00:08:30,948
Ms. Kang.

134
00:08:36,412 --> 00:08:37,830
Were you crying?

135
00:08:50,593 --> 00:08:51,802
Mr. Park.

136
00:08:54,555 --> 00:08:57,767
My sister practically raised me.

137
00:08:59,185 --> 00:09:01,145
I thought that was only natural,

138
00:09:01,979 --> 00:09:04,106
but it feels like a luxury to me now.

139
00:09:06,108 --> 00:09:08,319
I have a debt like that too.

140
00:09:10,780 --> 00:09:12,615
There's someone

141
00:09:12,698 --> 00:09:15,660
who took me in and protected me
instead of my father.

142
00:09:18,245 --> 00:09:19,288
He…

143
00:09:20,373 --> 00:09:22,208
doesn't want anything in return,

144
00:09:23,626 --> 00:09:25,544
but I still want to repay him.

145
00:09:27,380 --> 00:09:29,090
It's not because I feel indebted,

146
00:09:30,299 --> 00:09:31,467
but because I'm grateful.

147
00:09:34,095 --> 00:09:35,596
It was heartwarming.

148
00:09:38,099 --> 00:09:38,933
However,

149
00:09:40,142 --> 00:09:41,644
do you know that such debts

150
00:09:42,478 --> 00:09:45,898
sometimes give us the motivation to go on?

151
00:09:48,150 --> 00:09:49,026
You're right.

152
00:09:51,112 --> 00:09:53,906
But now,

153
00:09:53,989 --> 00:09:57,201
I'm not even sure if my dream
is actually mine

154
00:09:57,284 --> 00:09:59,078
or my sister's.

155
00:09:59,829 --> 00:10:03,040
My failure feels like
my sister's failure now.

156
00:10:04,125 --> 00:10:06,001
Isn't it okay to fail?

157
00:10:07,503 --> 00:10:09,171
Why should I fail?

158
00:10:09,797 --> 00:10:12,425
Some things grow clearer when you fail.

159
00:10:13,467 --> 00:10:16,762
You sometimes see things
that you weren't able to see before.

160
00:10:17,763 --> 00:10:20,850
Then what did you see after failing?

161
00:10:26,564 --> 00:10:27,481
People.

162
00:10:28,315 --> 00:10:30,067
The people who are protecting me,

163
00:10:30,735 --> 00:10:32,445
and the people I should protect.

164
00:10:37,825 --> 00:10:42,538
So you should take a look
at what you see after failing too.

165
00:10:47,585 --> 00:10:50,421
Why are you suddenly sounding so cool?

166
00:10:52,506 --> 00:10:53,924
YEONG-JU

167
00:10:54,008 --> 00:10:55,676
Oh, right. Yeong-ju!

168
00:10:56,635 --> 00:10:58,179
What do I do?

169
00:11:00,765 --> 00:11:03,058
SEOUL JUNGBU DETENTION CENTER

170
00:11:03,142 --> 00:11:06,645
<i>Inmate No. 3417, Park Yong-man,</i>
<i>is in the infirmary.</i>

171
00:11:06,729 --> 00:11:08,773
<i>No visitors are allowed</i>
<i>due to health reasons.</i>

172
00:11:20,451 --> 00:11:21,994
MR. SON, SEOUL POLICE CHIEF

173
00:11:30,628 --> 00:11:32,546
You asshole. Have you lost your mind?

174
00:11:32,630 --> 00:11:34,632
How dare you come here?

175
00:11:34,715 --> 00:11:37,593
Release Yong-man on medical bail first.

176
00:11:37,676 --> 00:11:40,346
-The money will be ready soon.
-It doesn't work that way.

177
00:11:40,429 --> 00:11:41,680
Bring the money first!

178
00:11:41,764 --> 00:11:43,807
He's sick!

179
00:11:43,891 --> 00:11:45,309
The elderly are always sick.

180
00:11:48,312 --> 00:11:49,730
If anything happens to him,

181
00:11:50,940 --> 00:11:52,191
you won't get your ten billion.

182
00:11:52,274 --> 00:11:54,485
Are you out of your mind?

183
00:11:55,653 --> 00:11:57,530
How dare you threaten me like that?

184
00:11:57,613 --> 00:11:59,156
Are you acting like a thug again?

185
00:11:59,240 --> 00:12:00,574
Damn it.

186
00:12:01,825 --> 00:12:03,077
You little brat.

187
00:12:13,420 --> 00:12:14,380
Mr. Park.

188
00:12:15,506 --> 00:12:16,674
Park Hae-kang.

189
00:12:17,341 --> 00:12:18,509
Get a grip.

190
00:12:24,265 --> 00:12:25,307
I can't get him released.

191
00:12:26,559 --> 00:12:28,769
But I'll let him get treatment outside.

192
00:12:28,852 --> 00:12:29,770
Anything else

193
00:12:29,853 --> 00:12:31,897
will be discussed
after you bring the money.

194
00:13:03,637 --> 00:13:06,682
The invisible hand is the president
of the construction company?

195
00:13:08,017 --> 00:13:09,351
He's something else.

196
00:13:09,435 --> 00:13:11,895
He's taking money
from the apartment complex that he built?

197
00:13:12,730 --> 00:13:13,814
How creative.

198
00:13:13,897 --> 00:13:16,567
But shouldn't we report this?

199
00:13:17,151 --> 00:13:19,486
Why don't you report all of us then?

200
00:13:20,446 --> 00:13:22,489
Oh, we were going to do
the same thing. Sorry.

201
00:13:22,573 --> 00:13:25,034
Boss, what are you planning to do now?

202
00:13:26,160 --> 00:13:27,202
First,

203
00:13:27,995 --> 00:13:30,623
I'm going to become
Lee Chung-won's vault keeper.

204
00:13:30,706 --> 00:13:32,583
-What?
-His keeper?

205
00:13:32,666 --> 00:13:33,500
Right.

206
00:13:33,584 --> 00:13:38,130
You need the vault's key
to steal that fund.

207
00:13:38,213 --> 00:13:42,051
But would Lee Chung-won
give you that position?

208
00:13:42,760 --> 00:13:44,595
I'll make sure he has no other choice.

209
00:13:45,804 --> 00:13:47,598
Let's go meet President Seo first.

210
00:13:48,098 --> 00:13:49,516
Go and look for him.

211
00:13:49,600 --> 00:13:51,018
-Yes, sir.
-Yes, sir.

212
00:14:07,326 --> 00:14:08,827
MAIL ARRIVAL NOTICE

213
00:14:16,043 --> 00:14:16,919
What is it?

214
00:14:17,836 --> 00:14:19,004
His card statement.

215
00:14:20,881 --> 00:14:23,175
But there aren't any recent transactions.

216
00:14:23,842 --> 00:14:25,886
He uses his card for everything.

217
00:14:27,221 --> 00:14:30,224
I can tell what's going on.

218
00:14:30,933 --> 00:14:31,892
What do you mean?

219
00:14:32,685 --> 00:14:33,644
It's just like me.

220
00:14:33,727 --> 00:14:35,354
I can't use my card either.

221
00:14:35,938 --> 00:14:38,774
Can't you track his location or anything?

222
00:14:38,857 --> 00:14:40,985
I can't. His phone is turned off.

223
00:14:41,068 --> 00:14:44,071
What? He really is doing
the exact same thing I'm doing.

224
00:14:44,655 --> 00:14:46,281
I can't turn on my phone either.

225
00:14:46,365 --> 00:14:47,992
I just leave it somewhere warm

226
00:14:48,075 --> 00:14:50,953
and use it to iron my clothes.

227
00:14:51,036 --> 00:14:52,830
Good for you.

228
00:14:53,497 --> 00:14:54,665
Wait.

229
00:14:54,748 --> 00:14:56,875
President Seo went on a trip abroad?

230
00:14:56,959 --> 00:14:58,460
I don't know.

231
00:14:58,544 --> 00:15:00,546
He just sent a text
saying he's going overseas.

232
00:15:00,629 --> 00:15:02,381
He betrayed us.

233
00:15:02,464 --> 00:15:05,676
Traveling abroad
after the mess he created?

234
00:15:05,759 --> 00:15:07,094
Just forget him.

235
00:15:08,345 --> 00:15:11,682
We've decided to side
with the new president now,

236
00:15:11,765 --> 00:15:15,519
so please put in a good word for us
with President Park.

237
00:15:17,312 --> 00:15:18,939
You can rely on me.

238
00:15:19,023 --> 00:15:21,567
I'm Hae-kang's right-hand man.

239
00:15:21,650 --> 00:15:23,402
Is that so?

240
00:15:23,485 --> 00:15:25,988
Would you like to have anything else?

241
00:15:29,700 --> 00:15:30,784
Then can I order

242
00:15:30,868 --> 00:15:33,203
another large tea?

243
00:15:34,329 --> 00:15:36,707
You might feel sick
from a blood sugar spike.

244
00:15:36,790 --> 00:15:38,208
Drink some water. Water, please.

245
00:15:38,292 --> 00:15:39,752
Get us a big cup of water.

246
00:15:39,835 --> 00:15:42,004
Please give us another big cup of tea.

247
00:15:42,838 --> 00:15:44,048
-This too.
-Rice cakes.

248
00:15:44,131 --> 00:15:45,883
More rice cakes too!

249
00:15:48,844 --> 00:15:50,804
-President Seo?
-Yes.

250
00:15:51,472 --> 00:15:54,433
What kind of work did he normally do here?

251
00:15:55,392 --> 00:15:57,352
I'd like to learn what he did

252
00:15:57,436 --> 00:15:59,354
and think about what to do
as the president--

253
00:15:59,438 --> 00:16:00,689
Geez.

254
00:16:02,357 --> 00:16:04,860
Just thinking about that asshole

255
00:16:04,943 --> 00:16:08,072
makes my blood pressure rise
and gives me a headache.

256
00:16:08,155 --> 00:16:11,784
He was acting as though
he were True Value's king…

257
00:16:11,867 --> 00:16:12,785
King?

258
00:16:15,162 --> 00:16:18,749
If I wrote down
every terrible thing he did,

259
00:16:18,832 --> 00:16:21,710
there would be enough
for a full-length novel.

260
00:16:21,794 --> 00:16:25,589
I'm not even sure where I should start.

261
00:16:25,672 --> 00:16:27,633
Right. The most ridiculous one.

262
00:16:27,716 --> 00:16:31,136
He bought water with the maintenance fees.

263
00:16:33,013 --> 00:16:36,517
He ordered water every month
with the fees,

264
00:16:36,600 --> 00:16:39,978
<i>and when they were delivered</i>
<i>to the office,</i>

265
00:16:40,062 --> 00:16:43,899
<i>the security guards</i>
<i>brought them to his house.</i>

266
00:16:44,441 --> 00:16:45,984
To his house?

267
00:16:46,068 --> 00:16:47,402
Seriously,

268
00:16:47,486 --> 00:16:50,322
it's not like water costs a fortune.

269
00:16:50,405 --> 00:16:51,782
How cheap is that?

270
00:16:51,865 --> 00:16:54,409
And does he think the guards
are his errand boys?

271
00:16:54,493 --> 00:16:55,577
He orders them around.

272
00:16:55,661 --> 00:16:59,206
His abuse of power is on another level.

273
00:17:00,916 --> 00:17:03,085
And you know what's really funny?

274
00:17:03,877 --> 00:17:07,631
Did you know that the cleaning staff

275
00:17:07,714 --> 00:17:10,968
have been growing gardens on the rooftops?

276
00:17:11,051 --> 00:17:14,054
No. There are gardens on the rooftops?

277
00:17:14,638 --> 00:17:18,725
At first, I thought
they were just doing that as a hobby,

278
00:17:18,809 --> 00:17:21,186
so I was going to turn a blind eye.

279
00:17:21,270 --> 00:17:22,146
-But…
-Yes?

280
00:17:22,229 --> 00:17:24,231
It turns out that they were delivering

281
00:17:24,314 --> 00:17:26,650
all the vegetables from their gardens

282
00:17:26,733 --> 00:17:29,528
to President Seo's house.

283
00:17:30,821 --> 00:17:32,656
He didn't even let them use pesticides

284
00:17:32,739 --> 00:17:34,867
because he wanted
to eat organic vegetables.

285
00:17:34,950 --> 00:17:37,870
<i>And the cleaning staff were too scared</i>
<i>of getting fired to protest.</i>

286
00:17:37,953 --> 00:17:41,039
<i>They were farming</i>
<i>on top of all the cleaning work.</i>

287
00:17:41,123 --> 00:17:43,167
How can we call him human?

288
00:17:43,250 --> 00:17:46,753
But you didn't say anything
when he was doing all that?

289
00:17:46,837 --> 00:17:49,089
Why wouldn't I?
I'm Jang Suk-jin, you know.

290
00:17:49,173 --> 00:17:50,382
Of course, I said something.

291
00:17:50,465 --> 00:17:52,801
But that bastard didn't even blink an eye.

292
00:17:54,052 --> 00:17:56,388
I could talk about this endlessly.

293
00:17:56,471 --> 00:17:59,183
But do you know the worst thing

294
00:17:59,266 --> 00:18:00,350
about President Seo?

295
00:18:01,185 --> 00:18:04,646
He opposes every single thing

296
00:18:04,730 --> 00:18:07,065
that the residents request or suggest.

297
00:18:07,149 --> 00:18:08,275
2021, RESIDENTS' ASSOCIATION MEETING

298
00:18:08,358 --> 00:18:10,527
Why do they keep refusing
to do the repairs?

299
00:18:11,195 --> 00:18:15,032
It seems like the construction company
thinks we're pushovers.

300
00:18:15,115 --> 00:18:17,868
We have to do something about this,
don't you think?

301
00:18:17,951 --> 00:18:19,661
-Right.
-He's right.

302
00:18:19,745 --> 00:18:22,831
I understand what you mean,

303
00:18:22,915 --> 00:18:24,875
but we're up against a large company.

304
00:18:24,958 --> 00:18:28,712
Can you guarantee
that we'll win a lawsuit against them?

305
00:18:28,795 --> 00:18:31,882
And if word spreads
about our apartments having defects,

306
00:18:31,965 --> 00:18:33,592
property values will drop.

307
00:18:33,675 --> 00:18:35,135
Will you be okay with that?

308
00:18:36,470 --> 00:18:38,847
A new seafood stew place opened nearby.

309
00:18:38,931 --> 00:18:42,643
I'll give you a detailed explanation
over dinner there later.

310
00:18:42,726 --> 00:18:44,019
So please, sit down.

311
00:18:52,194 --> 00:18:54,154
In any case,

312
00:18:54,238 --> 00:18:57,908
President Seo was a pro
at stopping  anyone from filing a lawsuit.

313
00:18:58,867 --> 00:19:00,869
And he harassed all the building reps

314
00:19:00,953 --> 00:19:02,412
who had any complaints

315
00:19:02,496 --> 00:19:06,333
and made them all give up
and move away in the end.

316
00:19:06,416 --> 00:19:11,463
Then he placed his own people
in those empty seats.

317
00:19:11,546 --> 00:19:14,549
He's a filthy fraud.

318
00:19:14,633 --> 00:19:18,011
Just thinking about him
makes my blood boil.

319
00:19:19,888 --> 00:19:21,306
<i>He stopped the lawsuits</i>

320
00:19:21,390 --> 00:19:24,768
<i>against Lee Chung-won's companies</i>
<i>and protected his money.</i>

321
00:19:24,851 --> 00:19:28,063
My keeper only has one job.

322
00:19:28,939 --> 00:19:30,232
To keep my money safe.

323
00:19:31,149 --> 00:19:32,985
<i>I get what I have to do,</i>

324
00:19:33,068 --> 00:19:35,487
<i>but will that be enough</i>
<i>to become one of his men?</i>

325
00:19:38,365 --> 00:19:41,076
<i>I need something with real impact.</i>

326
00:19:42,286 --> 00:19:44,246
<i>Something big.</i>

327
00:19:47,791 --> 00:19:49,001
Hello, ma'am.

328
00:19:50,877 --> 00:19:52,129
Hello.

329
00:19:53,463 --> 00:19:54,840
Were you buying groceries?

330
00:19:56,883 --> 00:19:57,884
Yes.

331
00:19:57,968 --> 00:20:00,846
We have business in Complex 2,
so excuse us.

332
00:20:00,929 --> 00:20:03,265
Bye. Take care, ma'am.

333
00:20:07,144 --> 00:20:08,770
She's so cold.

334
00:20:10,230 --> 00:20:11,857
Well, I'm the one at fault.

335
00:20:13,233 --> 00:20:15,277
Do I have to sleep
at Yeong-ju's again tonight?

336
00:20:22,951 --> 00:20:24,036
Wait!

337
00:20:26,538 --> 00:20:27,664
Were you out?

338
00:20:27,748 --> 00:20:29,041
I went to the supermarket.

339
00:20:29,541 --> 00:20:30,834
I got some boneless mackerel.

340
00:20:30,917 --> 00:20:34,671
Mr. Hwang said it's hard to debone fish
because of his eyesight.

341
00:20:35,339 --> 00:20:36,465
Who's Mr. Hwang?

342
00:20:37,632 --> 00:20:41,053
The man you call the Lizard
and treat harshly.

343
00:20:43,388 --> 00:20:46,266
You should've told Big Guy
to run errands like that.

344
00:20:46,767 --> 00:20:49,811
He said something about boneless fish
not being real fish,

345
00:20:49,895 --> 00:20:51,813
so he can't feed it to the kid.

346
00:20:51,897 --> 00:20:53,940
He has some weird philosophy about it.

347
00:20:54,024 --> 00:20:57,152
Big Guy has some serious opinions
when it comes to food.

348
00:20:57,652 --> 00:21:00,030
Life isn't that complicated though.

349
00:21:00,113 --> 00:21:02,157
We're just paying for convenience.

350
00:21:02,240 --> 00:21:03,241
What's the big deal?

351
00:21:09,581 --> 00:21:10,457
Are you okay?

352
00:21:23,011 --> 00:21:24,179
Excuse me.

353
00:21:24,262 --> 00:21:26,723
The elevator in Building 114 is broken.

354
00:21:26,807 --> 00:21:29,351
The president's in here.
Please take care of this quickly.

355
00:21:29,434 --> 00:21:30,894
<i>Just a moment, ma'am.</i>

356
00:21:34,940 --> 00:21:35,899
That startled me.

357
00:21:36,566 --> 00:21:39,569
I heard the elevators
are always breaking down.

358
00:21:40,070 --> 00:21:42,614
You're the president.
Can't you take care of this?

359
00:21:42,697 --> 00:21:43,990
You could just replace them all.

360
00:21:44,074 --> 00:21:46,743
The long-term repair reserve fund
shouldn't be used so rashly.

361
00:21:47,452 --> 00:21:48,662
Rashly?

362
00:21:48,745 --> 00:21:50,872
You're resolving
an inconvenience with money.

363
00:21:51,456 --> 00:21:53,959
Imagine having to use the stairs
every day instead.

364
00:21:54,042 --> 00:21:56,628
Everyone will be demanding
that the fund be used.

365
00:21:57,462 --> 00:21:59,923
Koreans can't stand any inconvenience.

366
00:22:00,006 --> 00:22:02,801
They'll gladly pay
to make life more convenient.

367
00:22:03,468 --> 00:22:06,888
They buy convenience,
like this boneless mackerel.

368
00:22:12,185 --> 00:22:13,353
It's working now.

369
00:22:14,980 --> 00:22:15,814
Let's go.

370
00:22:22,070 --> 00:22:23,363
RESIDENTS' ASSOCIATION MEETING

371
00:22:23,447 --> 00:22:24,823
Thank you for your suggestions.

372
00:22:24,906 --> 00:22:25,907
To summarize,

373
00:22:25,991 --> 00:22:28,452
replacing the equipment
in the community center gym,

374
00:22:28,535 --> 00:22:31,496
toys for the kids cafe,
a donation to the senior center,

375
00:22:31,580 --> 00:22:33,832
and repainting the exterior walls.

376
00:22:33,915 --> 00:22:36,251
Yes, those are the main suggestions.

377
00:22:36,334 --> 00:22:37,502
All right.

378
00:22:37,586 --> 00:22:39,379
The suggestions you've made

379
00:22:39,462 --> 00:22:41,089
are about making a better environment

380
00:22:41,173 --> 00:22:43,300
and improving resident services here.

381
00:22:43,383 --> 00:22:46,887
I also believe
all of these things are necessary.

382
00:22:46,970 --> 00:22:49,639
But to resolve all these problems,

383
00:22:49,723 --> 00:22:51,308
you know we need money, don't you?

384
00:22:53,226 --> 00:22:54,603
It all requires money.

385
00:22:54,686 --> 00:22:55,645
Money's the problem.

386
00:22:56,313 --> 00:22:59,274
That is why I'm suggesting
a 100% increase in the reserve fund

387
00:22:59,983 --> 00:23:03,111
for the present and future
of our apartment complex.

388
00:23:03,195 --> 00:23:04,863
What? 100%?

389
00:23:04,946 --> 00:23:06,072
100%?

390
00:23:07,407 --> 00:23:08,909
Isn't 100% too much?

391
00:23:12,078 --> 00:23:14,706
What? A 100% increase?

392
00:23:14,789 --> 00:23:16,458
What's gotten into him?

393
00:23:16,541 --> 00:23:19,044
What the heck is he thinking?

394
00:23:19,127 --> 00:23:21,254
That took quite a surprising turn.

395
00:23:21,338 --> 00:23:23,965
It does make me look forward
to the next episode.

396
00:23:26,801 --> 00:23:27,677
Yes, go on.

397
00:23:28,428 --> 00:23:30,388
Can't we cover
all the proposals from today

398
00:23:30,472 --> 00:23:33,475
with the reserve fund
that we already have right now?

399
00:23:33,558 --> 00:23:36,102
This apartment complex
is nearly ten years old now.

400
00:23:36,186 --> 00:23:37,771
More and more repairs will be needed.

401
00:23:37,854 --> 00:23:40,482
If we keep using
the reserve fund every time,

402
00:23:40,565 --> 00:23:42,275
we won't have anything left.

403
00:23:42,901 --> 00:23:45,362
To invest in improving
our living environment

404
00:23:45,445 --> 00:23:48,073
and carry out future repair plans,

405
00:23:48,156 --> 00:23:51,284
an increase in the reserve fund fee
is inevitable.

406
00:23:52,994 --> 00:23:53,912
Excuse me.

407
00:23:53,995 --> 00:23:56,873
I get all that,

408
00:23:56,957 --> 00:23:59,084
but if you're going to increase the fee,

409
00:23:59,167 --> 00:24:01,753
-you should do it gradually.
-Exactly.

410
00:24:01,836 --> 00:24:05,090
You can't just increase it
by 100% so suddenly.

411
00:24:05,173 --> 00:24:07,300
-That's a bit too much.
-Yeah.

412
00:24:08,426 --> 00:24:09,678
Our apartment complex

413
00:24:09,761 --> 00:24:12,472
has never raised the fee
since it was occupied.

414
00:24:12,555 --> 00:24:15,809
If you factor in inflation,
the amount hasn't changed on paper,

415
00:24:15,892 --> 00:24:18,853
but its real value
has been decreasing every year.

416
00:24:19,437 --> 00:24:20,563
To put it simply,

417
00:24:20,647 --> 00:24:24,192
you've been getting a discount
on the fee every year.

418
00:24:24,276 --> 00:24:28,154
Well, you're not wrong,

419
00:24:28,238 --> 00:24:29,155
but still…

420
00:24:29,239 --> 00:24:31,366
We live in a large apartment complex.

421
00:24:31,449 --> 00:24:34,619
Even a small repair
would be a huge project.

422
00:24:35,203 --> 00:24:36,746
With the reserve fund we have now,

423
00:24:36,830 --> 00:24:39,291
we won't be fully prepared
for future maintenance.

424
00:24:40,375 --> 00:24:42,460
But nothing is that urgent right now.

425
00:24:42,544 --> 00:24:44,713
A 100% increase is too much.

426
00:24:44,796 --> 00:24:45,755
That's what I'm saying.

427
00:24:46,881 --> 00:24:49,801
But President Park does have a point.

428
00:24:50,635 --> 00:24:52,512
There are apartment complexes
similar to ours,

429
00:24:52,595 --> 00:24:55,056
but they have much higher fees.

430
00:24:56,224 --> 00:24:58,601
-Yeah.
-Right.

431
00:25:01,438 --> 00:25:02,856
I agree as well.

432
00:25:02,939 --> 00:25:06,276
More and more problems
will come up as time passes,

433
00:25:06,943 --> 00:25:09,571
so it won't be a bad idea
to prepare in advance.

434
00:25:09,654 --> 00:25:10,822
-Right?
-Yes.

435
00:25:12,741 --> 00:25:14,034
You're right.

436
00:25:14,117 --> 00:25:17,746
If it's never been increased before,
I guess it's about time.

437
00:25:17,829 --> 00:25:20,957
Prices have gone up a lot over the years.

438
00:25:21,041 --> 00:25:24,377
Still, I believe
a 100% increase is too much.

439
00:25:24,461 --> 00:25:26,629
Right. I understand
your reason for opposing.

440
00:25:26,713 --> 00:25:28,965
That's why I'd like to hold

441
00:25:29,632 --> 00:25:31,926
a residents' vote this weekend.

442
00:25:32,427 --> 00:25:35,180
A residents' vote. That's a good idea.

443
00:25:36,389 --> 00:25:38,308
He's forward-thinking.

444
00:25:42,187 --> 00:25:45,190
But do you really agree
to raising the reserve fund fee?

445
00:25:45,273 --> 00:25:46,483
Of course not!

446
00:25:47,525 --> 00:25:48,902
Then why?

447
00:25:49,402 --> 00:25:51,446
We need to get on his good side.

448
00:25:51,529 --> 00:25:54,074
We have to show him
that we're all on his side

449
00:25:54,157 --> 00:25:56,242
to win some brownie points.

450
00:25:57,327 --> 00:25:59,871
But what if he really increases the fee?

451
00:25:59,954 --> 00:26:01,623
It's a 100% increase.

452
00:26:01,706 --> 00:26:04,709
He can't. We're doing a vote.

453
00:26:04,793 --> 00:26:07,003
The residents aren't crazy.

454
00:26:07,087 --> 00:26:09,047
Why would they agree to that?

455
00:26:09,130 --> 00:26:12,258
Then we just have to pretend
to support his proposal,

456
00:26:12,342 --> 00:26:14,677
-then vote against it.
-That's right.

457
00:26:17,764 --> 00:26:20,683
A proposal to raise
the reserve fund fee by 100%?

458
00:26:22,560 --> 00:26:24,562
Is this the plan you prepared?

459
00:26:24,646 --> 00:26:26,022
A meaningless vote?

460
00:26:26,106 --> 00:26:28,691
Boss, this really doesn't make any sense.

461
00:26:28,775 --> 00:26:29,859
It's impossible.

462
00:26:29,943 --> 00:26:32,278
It's the cost of a whole chicken
plus cheese balls.

463
00:26:32,779 --> 00:26:34,322
It's way too much.

464
00:26:34,406 --> 00:26:35,573
Just wait.

465
00:26:37,075 --> 00:26:38,743
More than half the residents

466
00:26:39,661 --> 00:26:41,413
will vote yes in the end.

467
00:26:48,002 --> 00:26:49,462
When are you coming home?

468
00:26:50,213 --> 00:26:51,881
I'll come when I come.

469
00:26:51,965 --> 00:26:53,091
You brat.

470
00:26:54,342 --> 00:26:55,760
I told you not to wear this.

471
00:26:56,344 --> 00:26:58,721
-You're wearing it again?
-Mom, there are people here.

472
00:27:00,974 --> 00:27:01,975
What's going on?

473
00:27:02,058 --> 00:27:03,893
What? Did it just stop?

474
00:27:03,977 --> 00:27:06,396
Is this working? Hello?

475
00:27:07,439 --> 00:27:08,731
Mr. Choi!

476
00:27:09,524 --> 00:27:11,234
The elevator stopped!

477
00:27:12,735 --> 00:27:14,612
ELEVATOR UNDER MAINTENANCE

478
00:27:20,410 --> 00:27:22,787
Why is it so hard
just to smoke a cigarette?

479
00:27:25,999 --> 00:27:28,585
Mom, my legs hurt. Carry me.

480
00:27:28,668 --> 00:27:30,170
My legs hurt too.

481
00:27:30,253 --> 00:27:31,463
Carry me!

482
00:27:32,589 --> 00:27:33,548
We're late. Come on.

483
00:27:33,631 --> 00:27:36,134
-I'll be late for kindergarten!
-All right.

484
00:27:36,217 --> 00:27:37,802
There it is. Oh, hello.

485
00:27:38,678 --> 00:27:39,804
I can't believe this!

486
00:27:41,181 --> 00:27:43,224
-Why's it like this every day?
-You're so fast.

487
00:27:44,225 --> 00:27:46,227
Yes. Building 107? We're so sorry.

488
00:27:46,311 --> 00:27:47,687
We're checking right now.

489
00:27:47,770 --> 00:27:49,689
Yes, the repair company is on its way.

490
00:27:49,772 --> 00:27:51,024
Building 212 too?

491
00:27:51,107 --> 00:27:52,609
If you can wait just a moment…

492
00:27:52,692 --> 00:27:55,862
It's the first time
so many have broken down at once.

493
00:27:56,404 --> 00:27:58,823
Is the repair company still not answering?

494
00:28:00,116 --> 00:28:01,242
-Call them again.
-Okay.

495
00:28:03,203 --> 00:28:05,121
We'll do our best
to take care of this issue

496
00:28:05,205 --> 00:28:06,331
as soon as possible.

497
00:28:06,414 --> 00:28:08,416
-Come on.
-When?

498
00:28:10,418 --> 00:28:13,922
Everyone, we'll be able to take care
of this issue faster

499
00:28:14,005 --> 00:28:16,090
if you all head back first.

500
00:28:16,174 --> 00:28:18,468
-Do something about the elevators.
-Everyone.

501
00:28:18,551 --> 00:28:20,386
-Please.
-How will you take care of this?

502
00:28:20,470 --> 00:28:22,430
Are you even doing your jobs?

503
00:28:22,514 --> 00:28:24,390
We live on the 28th floor.

504
00:28:24,474 --> 00:28:27,268
Can you fix it before my kid comes home?

505
00:28:27,352 --> 00:28:30,355
Everyone, I'm a resident here as well.

506
00:28:30,438 --> 00:28:31,648
I had to walk too.

507
00:28:31,731 --> 00:28:34,859
If you give us time,
we'll handle this as soon as possible.

508
00:28:34,943 --> 00:28:36,986
Mr. Choi, let's call an emergency meeting.

509
00:28:37,070 --> 00:28:38,446
Yes, sir.

510
00:28:40,532 --> 00:28:42,033
That's not the problem right now.

511
00:28:42,116 --> 00:28:43,785
How will we go upstairs?

512
00:28:44,285 --> 00:28:47,455
RESIDENTS' ASSOCIATION
ELEVATOR BREAKDOWN RESPONSE MEETING

513
00:28:47,539 --> 00:28:48,873
How will you take care of this?

514
00:28:49,666 --> 00:28:52,418
Everyone, please calm down.

515
00:28:52,502 --> 00:28:54,462
Let's hear from our president first.

516
00:28:56,047 --> 00:28:57,215
To tell you the truth,

517
00:28:57,298 --> 00:29:00,552
because of a strike
at the factory overseas,

518
00:29:00,635 --> 00:29:02,720
they say it'll take a year
for the parts to arrive.

519
00:29:03,638 --> 00:29:06,057
-How can we wait a year?
-That makes no sense!

520
00:29:06,140 --> 00:29:07,433
How can we wait an entire year?

521
00:29:07,517 --> 00:29:09,310
Do something, President Park!

522
00:29:09,394 --> 00:29:11,604
We're checking with companies in Korea

523
00:29:11,688 --> 00:29:13,857
to see if anyone has the parts,

524
00:29:13,940 --> 00:29:15,191
so let's wait a bit longer.

525
00:29:16,192 --> 00:29:18,486
You're always just asking us to wait.

526
00:29:18,570 --> 00:29:20,363
-How long do we have to wait?
-Right?

527
00:29:20,446 --> 00:29:22,323
It might be fine
for those on the lower floors,

528
00:29:22,407 --> 00:29:24,909
but people living on higher floors
can't keep enduring this.

529
00:29:24,993 --> 00:29:27,078
This is ridiculous!

530
00:29:27,161 --> 00:29:29,664
My mother will collapse
climbing the stairs!

531
00:29:35,461 --> 00:29:36,921
That is why

532
00:29:37,005 --> 00:29:39,340
I am proposing
to replace all the elevators

533
00:29:39,424 --> 00:29:42,552
to prevent the continuous breakdowns

534
00:29:43,219 --> 00:29:45,555
and any future safety issues.

535
00:29:47,432 --> 00:29:48,641
I can't believe this.

536
00:29:48,725 --> 00:29:50,852
-That's easier said than done.
-Excuse me…

537
00:29:50,935 --> 00:29:52,103
-It takes time and money.
-So…

538
00:29:53,229 --> 00:29:56,232
That would cost a fortune.

539
00:29:56,316 --> 00:29:57,483
How would you pay for that?

540
00:29:57,567 --> 00:29:59,903
Is it possible
with the current reserve fund?

541
00:29:59,986 --> 00:30:00,945
You're right.

542
00:30:01,988 --> 00:30:04,032
Our reserve fund isn't enough.

543
00:30:04,908 --> 00:30:07,785
We currently have
about 17 billion in the fund,

544
00:30:07,869 --> 00:30:11,623
but we'd need approximately 20 billion
to replace the elevators

545
00:30:11,706 --> 00:30:13,541
in every building.

546
00:30:13,625 --> 00:30:14,876
Twenty billion?

547
00:30:14,959 --> 00:30:16,336
Oh my gosh.

548
00:30:16,419 --> 00:30:19,631
-Then we'd have to pay for the rest.
-President Park.

549
00:30:20,465 --> 00:30:24,093
You don't seem to be aware of this,

550
00:30:24,177 --> 00:30:28,932
but the elevators
have been breaking down for a long time.

551
00:30:29,015 --> 00:30:31,476
It's been like this
ever since we first moved here.

552
00:30:31,559 --> 00:30:33,019
-Exactly.
-Right.

553
00:30:33,102 --> 00:30:36,272
We should really just
file a lawsuit this time.

554
00:30:36,356 --> 00:30:37,941
Let's sue the company!

555
00:30:38,733 --> 00:30:40,068
We should!

556
00:30:42,070 --> 00:30:43,237
A lawsuit?

557
00:30:44,322 --> 00:30:46,866
The defect repair period is already over.

558
00:30:47,450 --> 00:30:50,119
I know it's upsetting,
but you should've done it sooner.

559
00:30:50,203 --> 00:30:51,329
You stayed quiet until now,

560
00:30:51,412 --> 00:30:54,415
but you blame the company
after the defect repair period is over?

561
00:30:54,499 --> 00:30:56,584
That would only look
like you're throwing a fit.

562
00:30:56,668 --> 00:30:58,920
What's more,
our opponent is a large company.

563
00:30:59,003 --> 00:31:03,257
They'll hire
the best law firm in Korea to fight us.

564
00:31:03,341 --> 00:31:05,385
And if we lose that fight,

565
00:31:05,468 --> 00:31:08,429
we'll all have to bear
the enormous cost of that lawsuit.

566
00:31:08,513 --> 00:31:10,056
Are you willing to take that risk?

567
00:31:14,811 --> 00:31:16,187
-I have a headache.
-Then…

568
00:31:16,938 --> 00:31:18,731
what are you suggesting?

569
00:31:20,149 --> 00:31:22,026
I am sincerely urging you

570
00:31:22,110 --> 00:31:25,446
to understand that an increase
in the reserve fund fee is inevitable.

571
00:31:26,739 --> 00:31:29,534
That damn reserve fund…

572
00:31:29,617 --> 00:31:31,077
We have to pay more?

573
00:31:35,915 --> 00:31:40,044
Everyone, will you buy convenience
for the cost of one chicken?

574
00:31:40,128 --> 00:31:42,422
Or will you keep living in fear,
riding an elevator

575
00:31:42,505 --> 00:31:44,382
that could break down at any moment?

576
00:31:45,591 --> 00:31:46,843
Your choice

577
00:31:48,094 --> 00:31:49,470
will change your future.

578
00:31:53,558 --> 00:31:55,601
I'm just going to vote yes.

579
00:31:56,102 --> 00:31:58,855
It's not like the reserve fund
is going to disappear.

580
00:31:58,938 --> 00:32:01,107
It's going back
into the apartment complex.

581
00:32:02,900 --> 00:32:04,652
No, I can't deliver it on foot.

582
00:32:04,736 --> 00:32:07,113
I'm on the first floor. Please come down.

583
00:32:09,615 --> 00:32:10,783
It's Unit 2802.

584
00:32:11,993 --> 00:32:12,994
Thank you.

585
00:32:14,328 --> 00:32:17,040
I'm getting delivery
because I don't want to cook,

586
00:32:17,123 --> 00:32:19,333
but this is going to kill my knees.

587
00:32:20,209 --> 00:32:22,128
Whatever. I'm just going to vote yes.

588
00:32:22,211 --> 00:32:26,090
How can the elderly live like this?

589
00:32:26,174 --> 00:32:28,342
-My goodness…
-Just a moment.

590
00:32:28,426 --> 00:32:30,970
Mother, let's get some rest here.

591
00:32:31,054 --> 00:32:32,680
Gosh, my knees.

592
00:32:36,684 --> 00:32:39,228
Money isn't the problem right now.

593
00:32:41,856 --> 00:32:43,149
Be careful.

594
00:32:43,232 --> 00:32:45,526
Did you hear they're doubling
the reserve fund fee?

595
00:32:45,610 --> 00:32:46,944
Yeah.

596
00:32:47,570 --> 00:32:49,280
Double the fee would be tough.

597
00:32:50,448 --> 00:32:52,742
We're only renting.

598
00:32:52,825 --> 00:32:54,911
Even if we pay it
and they replace the elevators,

599
00:32:54,994 --> 00:32:57,663
we can get all the fees back
when we move out.

600
00:32:58,331 --> 00:33:00,083
We have nothing to lose.

601
00:33:01,417 --> 00:33:02,293
Are you happy?

602
00:33:02,376 --> 00:33:04,212
Are you happy that we're renting?

603
00:33:04,712 --> 00:33:06,089
Yeah, I am.

604
00:33:09,092 --> 00:33:11,177
Why did the elevators have to break down

605
00:33:11,260 --> 00:33:13,054
right after President Park got elected?

606
00:33:13,137 --> 00:33:14,722
Those damn elevators.

607
00:33:16,182 --> 00:33:18,309
He could become a lame duck at this rate.

608
00:33:18,976 --> 00:33:20,019
What time is it?

609
00:33:21,562 --> 00:33:23,523
Gosh. Is the vote closed now?

610
00:33:40,832 --> 00:33:41,958
What time is it?

611
00:33:42,959 --> 00:33:44,794
It's 6:30.

612
00:33:45,294 --> 00:33:46,379
The vote closed at 6:00.

613
00:33:46,462 --> 00:33:48,464
The results should've
been out immediately.

614
00:33:48,965 --> 00:33:50,508
Why aren't they announcing it?

615
00:33:55,304 --> 00:33:57,932
I'll go to the office myself and check…

616
00:33:59,517 --> 00:34:01,519
<i>This is the management office.</i>

617
00:34:01,602 --> 00:34:03,229
<i>We'll announce the results</i>

618
00:34:03,312 --> 00:34:07,525
<i>of the vote on increasing</i>
<i>the long-term repair reserve fund fee.</i>

619
00:34:07,608 --> 00:34:11,237
<i>Of the 7,237 households</i>
<i>that participated in the vote,</i>

620
00:34:11,320 --> 00:34:13,698
<i>52.7% were in favor,</i>

621
00:34:13,781 --> 00:34:16,742
<i>-and 47.3% were against.</i>
-We did it.

622
00:34:16,826 --> 00:34:19,537
<i>The proposal to increase the fee</i>
<i>has been approved.</i>

623
00:34:32,258 --> 00:34:33,551
Double the reserve fund!

624
00:34:34,260 --> 00:34:36,053
Wow!

625
00:34:36,137 --> 00:34:38,472
Double the reserve fund fee!

626
00:34:41,392 --> 00:34:43,895
<i>The increased</i>
<i>long-term repair reserve fund fee</i>

627
00:34:43,978 --> 00:34:47,607
<i>will be reflected in the maintenance fees</i>
<i>starting this month.</i>

628
00:34:47,690 --> 00:34:50,735
<i>We kindly ask</i>
<i>for your support and cooperation.</i>

629
00:34:50,818 --> 00:34:53,070
<i>-Thank you.</i>
-Park Hae-kang is amazing.

630
00:34:53,779 --> 00:34:57,450
He really is quite the talent.

631
00:34:57,533 --> 00:35:00,203
He really increased the reserve fund fee.

632
00:35:00,786 --> 00:35:01,996
It seems…

633
00:35:02,788 --> 00:35:04,540
I've gotten

634
00:35:04,624 --> 00:35:08,085
a much better replacement.

635
00:35:10,379 --> 00:35:12,298
Sorry for asking to meet
at such a late hour.

636
00:35:13,049 --> 00:35:15,509
All the management companies
are yours, aren't they?

637
00:35:15,593 --> 00:35:18,846
Oh, I was trying
not to make it so obvious.

638
00:35:18,930 --> 00:35:19,889
Could you tell?

639
00:35:19,972 --> 00:35:22,099
Call the elevator repair company.

640
00:35:22,725 --> 00:35:23,726
Why?

641
00:35:23,809 --> 00:35:25,311
I need to stop the elevators.

642
00:35:25,394 --> 00:35:26,395
Why?

643
00:35:26,479 --> 00:35:27,980
I'm different from President Seo.

644
00:35:28,064 --> 00:35:30,066
Just keeping the money is no fun.

645
00:35:30,650 --> 00:35:31,943
I told you,

646
00:35:32,026 --> 00:35:34,111
just keeping it is hard enough.

647
00:35:34,195 --> 00:35:35,571
I'd like to increase it,

648
00:35:35,655 --> 00:35:37,240
not just protect it.

649
00:35:39,242 --> 00:35:40,451
My money?

650
00:35:50,127 --> 00:35:52,713
I did as you asked, Mr. Park.

651
00:35:53,464 --> 00:35:54,924
But isn't this a huge gamble?

652
00:35:55,508 --> 00:35:57,301
If it is, what would you bet on?

653
00:35:59,303 --> 00:36:00,221
I don't bet anything

654
00:36:00,304 --> 00:36:04,016
on something I'm not certain of.

655
00:36:04,684 --> 00:36:05,685
Gambling

656
00:36:05,768 --> 00:36:08,521
is what desperate people do.

657
00:36:11,274 --> 00:36:13,484
You must be quite anxious.

658
00:36:16,237 --> 00:36:17,989
You're more of a coward than I thought.

659
00:36:19,699 --> 00:36:23,202
I don't start any games
that I'm not confident in.

660
00:36:25,621 --> 00:36:26,789
You're very cool.

661
00:36:38,676 --> 00:36:41,721
Why does Park Hae-kang
keep making my heart flutter?

662
00:36:42,430 --> 00:36:43,931
This is bad.

663
00:36:44,598 --> 00:36:45,683
Oh, right.

664
00:36:45,766 --> 00:36:47,518
I have to do what he asked.

665
00:36:48,102 --> 00:36:49,687
I already called the company.

666
00:36:49,770 --> 00:36:52,440
They'll get the elevators
working again tonight.

667
00:36:53,441 --> 00:36:54,358
But…

668
00:36:54,942 --> 00:36:58,279
the residents won't just sit still
if you don't replace them.

669
00:37:01,157 --> 00:37:03,826
Park Hae-kang said we'd need 20 billion,

670
00:37:03,909 --> 00:37:06,537
so they'll wait
until it reaches that amount.

671
00:37:06,620 --> 00:37:08,247
And after that,

672
00:37:08,331 --> 00:37:10,875
we can just give another reason
to postpone it.

673
00:37:11,459 --> 00:37:13,002
People forget things easily.

674
00:37:14,128 --> 00:37:14,962
Yes, sir.

675
00:37:16,130 --> 00:37:18,382
-There's something to report.
-Go on.

676
00:37:18,466 --> 00:37:22,595
The man Park Hae-kang was meeting
was an official in the police.

677
00:37:23,346 --> 00:37:25,681
Chief of Investigation, Son Dae-un.

678
00:37:26,182 --> 00:37:29,101
He was the one who busted
Park's gambling den in Gangnam.

679
00:37:30,519 --> 00:37:32,772
Then why would they meet up secretly?

680
00:37:32,855 --> 00:37:34,607
It seems Chief Son

681
00:37:34,690 --> 00:37:37,735
is holding Park Yong-man,
the former Oasis Gang boss, hostage.

682
00:37:37,818 --> 00:37:40,404
He took Park Hae-kang in.

683
00:37:40,488 --> 00:37:43,240
Park Yong-man is currently being held
at a detention center.

684
00:37:47,119 --> 00:37:50,081
So that's why Park Hae-kang needed money.

685
00:37:50,164 --> 00:37:51,707
To get his old boss out.

686
00:37:52,208 --> 00:37:53,334
But sir,

687
00:37:53,918 --> 00:37:57,505
Chief Son is connected
to the commissioner.

688
00:37:58,923 --> 00:37:59,882
The commissioner?

689
00:37:59,965 --> 00:38:03,552
The commissioner who's desperate
to join our One Club?

690
00:38:04,345 --> 00:38:05,554
Yes, that's right.

691
00:38:09,141 --> 00:38:11,519
Things are getting very interesting.

692
00:38:12,728 --> 00:38:13,604
Mr. Kim.

693
00:38:14,939 --> 00:38:19,276
We're going to get
double the reserve fund fees now.

694
00:38:20,444 --> 00:38:23,197
Then there's another matter
to take care of.

695
00:38:23,864 --> 00:38:26,909
Let's leave after just five more minutes.

696
00:38:38,087 --> 00:38:40,923
What on earth is President Park thinking?

697
00:38:42,216 --> 00:38:43,426
Could he…

698
00:38:45,970 --> 00:38:49,014
be aware that we don't have the fund?

699
00:38:50,433 --> 00:38:52,518
No. He could never tell from the papers.

700
00:39:02,903 --> 00:39:04,029
Oh dear.

701
00:39:05,239 --> 00:39:07,324
You're working late.

702
00:39:11,704 --> 00:39:13,664
Ha-jeong, can I talk to you for a moment?

703
00:39:14,999 --> 00:39:16,584
Mr. Choi, sit down.

704
00:39:16,667 --> 00:39:18,335
We're a family.

705
00:39:18,419 --> 00:39:19,712
Come on. Sit.

706
00:39:26,635 --> 00:39:29,096
What is this about?

707
00:39:29,180 --> 00:39:31,307
We're working on the elevator issue…

708
00:39:31,390 --> 00:39:33,017
It's not about that.

709
00:39:34,393 --> 00:39:35,895
Sir…

710
00:39:36,979 --> 00:39:38,063
What is it?

711
00:39:39,231 --> 00:39:41,275
I'd like to come clean

712
00:39:42,443 --> 00:39:43,819
about something to you too.

713
00:39:45,404 --> 00:39:48,157
I really like the ledger
that you organized,

714
00:39:48,240 --> 00:39:49,867
Ms. Kang.

715
00:39:50,534 --> 00:39:53,370
Even to me, it seems flawless.

716
00:39:58,584 --> 00:39:59,668
It's me.

717
00:40:00,628 --> 00:40:02,213
The guy who's taking the reserve fund.

718
00:40:11,222 --> 00:40:14,016
You're making me embarrassed
with that reaction.

719
00:40:14,600 --> 00:40:16,060
I'm not here to startle you.

720
00:40:16,143 --> 00:40:18,312
I'm sorry if I shocked you.

721
00:40:19,563 --> 00:40:20,940
The thing is,

722
00:40:21,941 --> 00:40:24,818
I love the way you work, Ms. Kang.

723
00:40:25,945 --> 00:40:28,113
But I heard you wanted to quit.

724
00:40:31,200 --> 00:40:34,745
Was there anything that displeased you?

725
00:40:38,541 --> 00:40:39,875
Was the pay too small?

726
00:40:40,751 --> 00:40:42,586
No, it's nothing like that.

727
00:40:42,670 --> 00:40:43,754
Or…

728
00:40:43,837 --> 00:40:47,091
how about joining
Taesan Construction's finance team?

729
00:40:47,841 --> 00:40:49,718
It's a better workplace than this,

730
00:40:49,802 --> 00:40:52,429
and you can proudly tell your family
it's a large company.

731
00:40:53,347 --> 00:40:54,223
What do you say?

732
00:40:56,892 --> 00:40:57,935
Ms. Kang.

733
00:40:58,644 --> 00:41:01,939
I'm offering you a job right now.

734
00:41:02,022 --> 00:41:05,609
I'll give you twice your current salary.

735
00:41:05,693 --> 00:41:06,735
Why aren't you answering?

736
00:41:07,444 --> 00:41:09,029
He's asking you a question.

737
00:41:18,914 --> 00:41:20,791
I'M SORRY, HA-JEONG

738
00:41:20,874 --> 00:41:24,628
So you're supposed to draw your family?

739
00:41:25,129 --> 00:41:26,005
Yes.

740
00:41:27,339 --> 00:41:28,632
Let's see…

741
00:41:31,969 --> 00:41:33,637
Why have you been sighing all day?

742
00:41:33,721 --> 00:41:35,973
You're a young lady
with a whole future ahead of you.

743
00:41:37,391 --> 00:41:40,894
That future has already
turned into a tangled mess.

744
00:41:42,271 --> 00:41:44,273
You said you're a professional.

745
00:41:44,940 --> 00:41:47,735
You should stick to your role
and help your kid with his homework.

746
00:41:47,818 --> 00:41:50,279
Sometimes, moms can be depressed too.

747
00:41:50,362 --> 00:41:52,239
You and that smart mouth of yours…

748
00:41:54,992 --> 00:41:56,660
Ta-da. It's Dad, Park Hae-kang.

749
00:41:56,744 --> 00:41:58,162
It looks just like him, right?

750
00:41:58,245 --> 00:42:00,873
Isn't Park Hae-kang
a bit more handsome than that?

751
00:42:03,876 --> 00:42:06,795
Do you really have to correct him
even when you're depressed?

752
00:42:07,838 --> 00:42:10,799
Facts are important
to seven-year-olds, you know.

753
00:42:11,508 --> 00:42:12,509
Geez.

754
00:42:15,512 --> 00:42:16,430
You know

755
00:42:17,097 --> 00:42:19,141
I can't stand people being bad at stuff.

756
00:42:19,224 --> 00:42:21,810
Let's do your homework based on facts.

757
00:42:21,894 --> 00:42:23,103
Okay.

758
00:42:25,189 --> 00:42:26,815
What color should we use?

759
00:42:30,486 --> 00:42:33,030
But aren't you going home? It's past 6:00.

760
00:42:34,948 --> 00:42:36,408
I'm working overtime today.

761
00:42:36,492 --> 00:42:37,326
Overtime?

762
00:42:37,951 --> 00:42:39,495
Mr. Park makes you work overtime?

763
00:42:39,578 --> 00:42:42,665
That brat.
Just report him to the Ministry of Labor.

764
00:42:42,748 --> 00:42:45,167
No, this is voluntary overtime.

765
00:42:45,959 --> 00:42:47,836
You don't even like your job.

766
00:42:47,920 --> 00:42:50,130
What do you mean, "voluntary overtime"?

767
00:42:52,549 --> 00:42:55,302
If you're going to keep sighing,
just go home.

768
00:42:55,386 --> 00:42:58,263
Or at least tell me what's going on.

769
00:42:59,223 --> 00:43:00,891
I just have something on my mind.

770
00:43:02,559 --> 00:43:04,561
Uncle Big Guy…

771
00:43:23,205 --> 00:43:25,874
I'm thinking of transferring
to a place with a higher salary.

772
00:43:26,625 --> 00:43:27,501
You…

773
00:43:29,878 --> 00:43:31,213
should start studying again.

774
00:43:32,881 --> 00:43:34,758
Quit everything else

775
00:43:34,842 --> 00:43:36,552
and focus on your studies.

776
00:43:36,635 --> 00:43:38,262
I'll do whatever it takes to support you.

777
00:43:38,345 --> 00:43:39,722
Ha-jeong,

778
00:43:39,805 --> 00:43:42,099
just go live your own life.

779
00:43:42,182 --> 00:43:44,017
Stop worrying about mine.

780
00:43:44,101 --> 00:43:46,145
How can you say that to me?

781
00:43:46,228 --> 00:43:47,229
I can.

782
00:43:47,896 --> 00:43:49,523
I have to.

783
00:43:49,606 --> 00:43:52,735
Just please stop wasting your own life
to support mine.

784
00:43:53,277 --> 00:43:54,361
That's enough.

785
00:43:55,112 --> 00:43:56,321
Get back to your studies.

786
00:43:56,405 --> 00:43:58,407
You should take the bar exam again.

787
00:43:58,490 --> 00:44:00,242
I'll handle this on my own.

788
00:44:00,325 --> 00:44:01,160
Ha-ri!

789
00:44:03,871 --> 00:44:06,081
I'm really sorry I lied to you,

790
00:44:07,541 --> 00:44:09,001
but I'm not quitting this gig.

791
00:44:09,543 --> 00:44:10,544
What?

792
00:44:11,420 --> 00:44:12,379
Ha-jeong.

793
00:44:16,133 --> 00:44:17,760
I've already failed.

794
00:44:24,266 --> 00:44:26,477
So you should accept that too.

795
00:44:29,146 --> 00:44:30,355
Someone told me

796
00:44:31,690 --> 00:44:34,485
that there are things you see
only after you fail.

797
00:44:36,570 --> 00:44:37,654
And what I saw…

798
00:44:39,031 --> 00:44:41,241
is you.

799
00:44:41,325 --> 00:44:43,911
I saw your life
that's been tied down by me.

800
00:44:49,833 --> 00:44:51,752
-Ha-ri, I--
-I'm grateful.

801
00:44:52,669 --> 00:44:54,838
I'm really grateful for the youth

802
00:44:55,589 --> 00:44:57,174
that you wasted because of me.

803
00:44:59,468 --> 00:45:01,720
And I'm really sorry.

804
00:45:07,601 --> 00:45:09,394
I'm going to start over.

805
00:45:11,563 --> 00:45:13,482
I'll achieve my dream on my own now.

806
00:45:37,172 --> 00:45:38,799
Why am I even here?

807
00:45:41,760 --> 00:45:43,345
Why do you keep crying?

808
00:45:48,809 --> 00:45:51,853
The debt collectors
were pressuring me today.

809
00:45:56,233 --> 00:45:59,027
Don't worry about me and go home.

810
00:46:24,011 --> 00:46:25,804
Please let me stay the night.

811
00:46:35,147 --> 00:46:36,940
Boss, why are you…

812
00:46:39,151 --> 00:46:41,069
Ms. Kang, why are you…

813
00:46:41,153 --> 00:46:43,030
What?

814
00:46:46,575 --> 00:46:47,909
Everyone, get up!

815
00:46:48,410 --> 00:46:49,953
Come out here!

816
00:46:50,037 --> 00:46:51,246
-What?
-What is it?

817
00:46:51,330 --> 00:46:52,497
Everyone, come out here!

818
00:46:52,581 --> 00:46:53,624
What?

819
00:46:53,707 --> 00:46:56,335
-What is it?
-Did you two…

820
00:46:57,169 --> 00:46:58,211
-What?
-Did you two…

821
00:46:58,295 --> 00:46:59,713
What is it?

822
00:47:00,797 --> 00:47:02,382
I'll pretend I didn't see that.

823
00:47:02,466 --> 00:47:04,426
-No, it's not like that.
-You got the wrong idea.

824
00:47:04,509 --> 00:47:05,886
What's going on?

825
00:47:05,969 --> 00:47:07,512
What is it?

826
00:47:07,596 --> 00:47:10,515
Ms. Kang just came out of the bedroom.

827
00:47:12,517 --> 00:47:14,478
What's wrong with that?
They're both young.

828
00:47:14,561 --> 00:47:16,980
People had children even during wars.

829
00:47:17,064 --> 00:47:18,815
-What are you saying?
-Children?

830
00:47:18,899 --> 00:47:21,902
Boss, you can tell us the truth.

831
00:47:21,985 --> 00:47:23,153
You really…

832
00:47:23,236 --> 00:47:24,988
No, we were the ones who were clueless.

833
00:47:25,072 --> 00:47:27,199
We'll spend the night
somewhere else twice a week!

834
00:47:27,282 --> 00:47:29,451
-All of you, stop it!
-You brat…

835
00:47:29,534 --> 00:47:32,120
From an intermittent family
to a real family…

836
00:47:33,121 --> 00:47:34,331
A love story?

837
00:47:34,414 --> 00:47:35,999
-No, a soap opera!
-A soap opera!

838
00:47:36,958 --> 00:47:38,710
Let's give them some privacy today!

839
00:47:38,794 --> 00:47:40,629
-All right.
-Come on. Let's go.

840
00:47:43,048 --> 00:47:43,882
I had no idea.

841
00:47:46,635 --> 00:47:47,678
What?

842
00:47:48,345 --> 00:47:49,930
-Why…
-Bye, then.

843
00:47:50,013 --> 00:47:51,556
What's with you guys?

844
00:47:51,640 --> 00:47:52,891
We'll be back later.

845
00:47:55,394 --> 00:47:57,229
Hit the elevator button.

846
00:47:58,563 --> 00:47:59,564
Come here.

847
00:48:03,777 --> 00:48:04,611
Gosh.

848
00:48:23,338 --> 00:48:26,174
Gentlemen, have some snacks.

849
00:48:26,258 --> 00:48:27,843
Gather round.

850
00:48:27,926 --> 00:48:29,761
That must be tasty.

851
00:48:31,054 --> 00:48:32,305
Great timing. I was hungry.

852
00:48:32,389 --> 00:48:33,849
Come on.

853
00:48:37,769 --> 00:48:38,770
All right.

854
00:48:44,234 --> 00:48:47,028
I bought these from a restaurant
going viral on social media.

855
00:48:47,612 --> 00:48:48,739
I waited two hours.

856
00:48:52,284 --> 00:48:53,493
It was worth the wait.

857
00:48:54,453 --> 00:48:55,954
Let me pack any leftovers

858
00:48:56,037 --> 00:48:57,539
so I can give them to my wife.

859
00:48:59,916 --> 00:49:01,877
You have to be good to your wife
when you're old.

860
00:49:01,960 --> 00:49:03,462
She's your retirement plan.

861
00:49:04,463 --> 00:49:06,214
You must be in a good mood today.

862
00:49:07,466 --> 00:49:08,592
I am.

863
00:49:08,675 --> 00:49:10,886
But it's not because of you.

864
00:49:11,636 --> 00:49:13,096
You can listen while you eat.

865
00:49:13,638 --> 00:49:15,515
After a long wait,

866
00:49:16,516 --> 00:49:18,602
our Oman New Town project
is back on track.

867
00:49:18,685 --> 00:49:19,936
Let's drink to that.

868
00:49:21,146 --> 00:49:22,939
-Congratulations.
-Cheers!

869
00:49:28,487 --> 00:49:29,905
As promised,

870
00:49:29,988 --> 00:49:33,450
money will start pouring
into your pockets now.

871
00:49:33,533 --> 00:49:35,452
So who should you be good to?

872
00:49:35,535 --> 00:49:37,037
Your retirement

873
00:49:37,120 --> 00:49:39,998
isn't secured by a wife
who can cheat on you anytime.

874
00:49:40,999 --> 00:49:42,876
It's secured by money.

875
00:49:44,169 --> 00:49:46,671
I'll be the one
taking care of your future now,

876
00:49:47,255 --> 00:49:48,757
so you should be good to me.

877
00:49:48,840 --> 00:49:49,758
Don't you think?

878
00:49:50,258 --> 00:49:53,303
Right. You're better than my own son.

879
00:49:55,222 --> 00:49:56,681
You did a great job.

880
00:49:56,765 --> 00:49:59,184
Isn't it nice to have
construction resume again?

881
00:49:59,267 --> 00:50:02,229
Yes. Very nice.

882
00:50:05,315 --> 00:50:07,192
Getting everything handed to you.

883
00:50:12,197 --> 00:50:14,282
You're very lucky to have all that

884
00:50:14,866 --> 00:50:16,117
without lifting a finger.

885
00:50:17,160 --> 00:50:19,204
-Come on.
-Eat up, everyone.

886
00:50:21,790 --> 00:50:22,749
Sir.

887
00:50:23,583 --> 00:50:25,752
Commissioner Kwak Ju-gwon is here.

888
00:50:35,011 --> 00:50:36,429
What is this?

889
00:50:37,430 --> 00:50:41,434
I got these valuable ginseng roots
especially for you,

890
00:50:42,269 --> 00:50:44,437
hoping they'll help restore your energy.

891
00:50:50,735 --> 00:50:52,654
Ginseng doesn't agree with me.

892
00:50:52,737 --> 00:50:54,155
I have too much heat in my body.

893
00:50:54,906 --> 00:50:55,907
You can have them.

894
00:50:56,700 --> 00:50:57,742
Pardon?

895
00:50:59,077 --> 00:51:00,203
By the way,

896
00:51:00,871 --> 00:51:03,832
how's the ten billion won coming along?

897
00:51:05,041 --> 00:51:06,585
Yes, well…

898
00:51:07,085 --> 00:51:09,004
My men are getting it prepared.

899
00:51:09,087 --> 00:51:11,464
Your men? Not yourself?

900
00:51:11,548 --> 00:51:13,174
Well,

901
00:51:13,258 --> 00:51:14,968
there are friends helping me.

902
00:51:16,094 --> 00:51:17,512
So you're extorting it.

903
00:51:18,263 --> 00:51:21,016
Oh, goodness.

904
00:51:22,142 --> 00:51:23,852
Extorting?

905
00:51:23,935 --> 00:51:25,145
I'm just getting help.

906
00:51:25,937 --> 00:51:29,566
I built a lot of connections
during my years as a cop.

907
00:51:29,649 --> 00:51:32,068
And which of those connections

908
00:51:32,152 --> 00:51:34,487
is getting you ten billion won?

909
00:51:37,616 --> 00:51:39,367
It's a guy who used to run a gambling den.

910
00:51:39,451 --> 00:51:42,287
He's a pro when it comes to getting money.

911
00:51:44,456 --> 00:51:45,916
A guy who ran a gambling den?

912
00:51:45,999 --> 00:51:47,083
Yes.

913
00:51:52,380 --> 00:51:54,257
His name's Park Hae-kang.

914
00:51:54,966 --> 00:51:56,718
-Park Hoe-kwang?
-No.

915
00:51:57,344 --> 00:51:59,262
Hae-kang.

916
00:52:00,180 --> 00:52:02,015
-Park Hae-kang?
-Yes.

917
00:52:02,933 --> 00:52:05,936
How do you know such a competent guy?

918
00:52:07,771 --> 00:52:10,732
Can you introduce me to him later?

919
00:52:12,233 --> 00:52:14,194
Sure, I will.

920
00:52:15,111 --> 00:52:17,155
I'll leave this with you.

921
00:52:40,887 --> 00:52:41,930
President Park.

922
00:52:42,013 --> 00:52:44,933
The 100% increase in the reserve fund fee.

923
00:52:45,517 --> 00:52:47,936
I was really touched by what you achieved.

924
00:52:48,019 --> 00:52:51,064
Can I give you a hug?

925
00:52:58,363 --> 00:53:01,700
You're making my heart pound these days.

926
00:53:02,659 --> 00:53:03,910
I'm so excited.

927
00:53:10,125 --> 00:53:11,835
Is it your first time in a penthouse?

928
00:53:11,918 --> 00:53:13,294
It's nothing special.

929
00:53:13,378 --> 00:53:14,462
The ceiling's high,

930
00:53:14,546 --> 00:53:17,465
but besides that,
it's no different from other houses.

931
00:53:18,383 --> 00:53:20,385
So have I proven that I'm better

932
00:53:21,386 --> 00:53:22,470
than President Seo?

933
00:53:24,723 --> 00:53:26,224
Of course.

934
00:53:26,808 --> 00:53:28,309
Thinking back now,

935
00:53:28,393 --> 00:53:31,229
President Seo was really useless.

936
00:53:32,230 --> 00:53:33,231
Very incompetent.

937
00:53:34,065 --> 00:53:37,152
I despise incompetent people the most.

938
00:53:37,902 --> 00:53:40,155
Then will you let me be the keeper

939
00:53:40,739 --> 00:53:41,948
of your vault?

940
00:53:43,116 --> 00:53:46,661
You are the perfect man
to take on that position.

941
00:53:51,291 --> 00:53:52,584
I'll count on you.

942
00:53:53,084 --> 00:53:56,212
I believe we'll make a great team.

943
00:53:56,296 --> 00:53:57,297
Don't you agree?

944
00:54:07,849 --> 00:54:10,393
I do feel bad putting you to work

945
00:54:10,477 --> 00:54:14,064
as soon as you've joined me
without even a honeymoon period,

946
00:54:14,814 --> 00:54:17,358
but I have an urgent favor to ask you.

947
00:54:18,151 --> 00:54:19,027
Sure.

948
00:54:19,527 --> 00:54:20,779
It's nothing difficult.

949
00:54:21,446 --> 00:54:23,698
Just take some money from Mr. Kim

950
00:54:23,782 --> 00:54:26,785
and deliver it to an apartment complex
in Gunam City.

951
00:54:27,619 --> 00:54:31,456
It's actually another complex
that I'm skimming from.

952
00:54:32,582 --> 00:54:35,543
I'm just putting back the money
I took out of there.

953
00:54:36,544 --> 00:54:39,923
There's going to be an audit soon,
so I'll get it back afterward.

954
00:54:41,466 --> 00:54:42,550
I understand.

955
00:54:43,718 --> 00:54:47,472
This is actually
what President Seo used to do.

956
00:54:47,555 --> 00:54:50,141
So think of this as training for the job.

957
00:54:51,184 --> 00:54:52,435
I'm counting on you.

958
00:55:16,751 --> 00:55:18,753
-Hey, Gyeong-nam.
<i>-Boss.</i>

959
00:55:18,837 --> 00:55:20,797
We tracked President Seo's whereabouts,

960
00:55:20,880 --> 00:55:23,216
and the last signal from his phone
came from Taegowon.

961
00:55:24,634 --> 00:55:26,219
-Taegowon?
<i>-Yes.</i>

962
00:55:26,803 --> 00:55:29,139
Je-gil hacked the security cams there,

963
00:55:29,764 --> 00:55:32,433
but he didn't ever see him
leave the premises.

964
00:55:33,351 --> 00:55:35,353
<i>It seems like President Seo was taken out.</i>

965
00:55:36,229 --> 00:55:37,230
<i>And…</i>

966
00:55:37,313 --> 00:55:39,899
his entire family disappeared as well.

967
00:55:40,733 --> 00:55:41,985
-Disappeared?
<i>-Yes.</i>

968
00:55:42,068 --> 00:55:45,488
Their belongings are still there,
but his family's gone.

969
00:55:45,572 --> 00:55:48,074
<i>It's like someone just erased them.</i>

970
00:55:48,908 --> 00:55:49,784
<i>Boss,</i>

971
00:55:50,702 --> 00:55:52,287
becoming Lee Chung-won's vault keeper

972
00:55:53,496 --> 00:55:54,747
is dangerous.

973
00:55:57,000 --> 00:55:59,878
Just stop digging
into President Seo for now.

974
00:55:59,961 --> 00:56:01,296
All right.

975
00:56:06,593 --> 00:56:08,011
Taegowon…

976
00:56:48,635 --> 00:56:50,094
KIM HONG-HYEON

977
00:56:51,596 --> 00:56:52,764
LEE JAE-GU

978
00:57:07,862 --> 00:57:10,281
SEO GANG-WON

979
00:57:24,170 --> 00:57:26,756
There are names for each of the trees.
What are they?

980
00:57:29,092 --> 00:57:31,594
They're people who sacrificed themselves
for Taegowon.

981
00:57:32,262 --> 00:57:35,431
So they're like commemorative trees.

982
00:57:40,103 --> 00:57:40,937
This is ten billion.

983
00:58:12,135 --> 00:58:13,386
<i>I can't get him released.</i>

984
00:58:13,469 --> 00:58:15,471
But I'll let him get treatment outside.

985
00:58:15,972 --> 00:58:16,806
Anything else

986
00:58:16,889 --> 00:58:18,933
will be discussed
after you bring the money.

987
00:58:25,773 --> 00:58:27,358
MR. SON, SEOUL POLICE CHIEF

988
00:58:29,444 --> 00:58:30,403
Yes?

989
00:58:30,486 --> 00:58:32,488
<i>Hey, Mr. Park.</i>

990
00:58:32,572 --> 00:58:35,825
Did you know
Park Yong-man was terminally ill?

991
00:58:46,628 --> 00:58:48,504
Hey, you can't just stop like that!

992
00:58:54,844 --> 00:58:56,095
What did you just say?

993
00:58:58,890 --> 00:58:59,932
<i>You didn't know?</i>

994
00:59:00,016 --> 00:59:01,643
They say it's pancreatic cancer.

995
00:59:01,726 --> 00:59:03,311
He has about three months left.

996
00:59:04,145 --> 00:59:05,313
<i>So…</i>

997
00:59:05,396 --> 00:59:07,815
you'd better hurry
if you don't want him to die in there.

998
00:59:07,899 --> 00:59:08,941
<i>Get the ten billion.</i>

999
00:59:12,195 --> 00:59:15,198
So the commissioner attacked Park Hae-kang

1000
00:59:15,281 --> 00:59:17,283
to give me ten billion won,

1001
00:59:17,367 --> 00:59:20,620
and that's why Park Hae-kang
was trying to take ten billion

1002
00:59:21,204 --> 00:59:23,665
from the reserve fund
in my apartment complex?

1003
00:59:24,540 --> 00:59:26,084
Mr. Kim,

1004
00:59:26,751 --> 00:59:31,005
I think I could get
the competent Park Hae-kang for free.

1005
00:59:32,048 --> 00:59:34,592
Do you trust Park Hae-kang?

1006
00:59:36,135 --> 00:59:38,137
I'm going to do one last test…

1007
00:59:40,682 --> 00:59:43,267
to see if I can trust him or not.

1008
00:59:57,490 --> 01:00:00,576
I'm bringing over the ten billion,
so release him.

1009
01:00:00,660 --> 01:00:01,828
Right now!

1010
01:00:10,837 --> 01:00:13,548
THE APARTMENT JOB

1011
01:00:37,655 --> 01:00:40,783
<i>Hey, did you know that there are people</i>
<i>using our community sauna for free?</i>

1012
01:00:40,867 --> 01:00:42,452
<i>-We use our cards to enter.</i>
-Unbelievable.

1013
01:00:42,535 --> 01:00:43,536
<i>You should see this.</i>

1014
01:00:43,619 --> 01:00:45,496
A complaint about people
using our facilities.

1015
01:00:45,580 --> 01:00:48,499
<i>-They want a facial recognition system.</i>
-I can't do this any longer.

1016
01:00:48,583 --> 01:00:49,876
<i>Use the reserve fund?</i>

1017
01:00:49,959 --> 01:00:51,169
-No.
-No.

1018
01:00:51,252 --> 01:00:53,629
<i>We need to find the people</i>
<i>and give them a warning.</i>

1019
01:00:53,713 --> 01:00:54,964
It's a rental unit.

1020
01:00:55,047 --> 01:00:57,675
<i>"Reveal the rental units." Nonsense.</i>

1021
01:00:57,759 --> 01:00:59,969
<i>The rental units are the problem.</i>

1022
01:01:00,678 --> 01:01:03,139
-Conflict.
<i>-Ms. Kang, can you work overtime today?</i>

1023
01:01:03,222 --> 01:01:04,599
<i>Why Park Hae-kang?</i>

1024
01:01:04,682 --> 01:01:08,311
<i>Park Hae-kang can see the bigger picture.</i>

1025
01:01:08,394 --> 01:01:09,437
Can you do something for me?

1026
01:01:09,520 --> 01:01:11,522
And when it's over,
I'll give you the ten billion.

1027
01:01:11,606 --> 01:01:13,524
<i>You'd better hurry,</i>

1028
01:01:13,608 --> 01:01:16,986
<i>because that ten billion you want</i>
<i>is on borrowed time too.</i>

1029
01:01:19,864 --> 01:01:21,866
Subtitle translation by: Juyoung Park

